{title: O Come, All Ye Faithful}
{artist: John Francis Wade / Frederick Oakeley}
{genre: Christmas}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Carol}
{key: G}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 122장}
{title_ko: 참 반가운 성도여}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 4/4}
{score: o-come-all-ye-faithful.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
O [G]come, all ye [D]faithful, joyful and tri[G]umphant
O [G]come ye, O [D]come ye to Beth[G]lehem
[Em]Come and be[D]hold Him, born the King of [G]angels
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [G]come, let us a[D]dore Him
O [G]come, let us a[D]dore Him
O [G]come, let us a[C]dore [G]Him
Christ the [D]Lord[G]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
God of [G]God, Light of [D]Light
Lo, He abhors not the [G]Virgin's womb
Very [Em]God, begotten [D]not created
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Sing, [G]choirs of [D]angels, sing in exul[G]tation
Sing, [G]all ye citi[D]zens of heaven a[G]bove
[Em]Glory to [D]God, in the high[G]est
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Yea, [G]Lord, we greet [D]Thee, born this happy [G]morning
[G]Jesus, to Thee be [D]glory [G]given
[Em]Word of the [D]Father, now in flesh ap[G]pearing
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
